  "title": "Emancipation of the Russian serfs",
  "summary": "On 3 March 1861 (19 February in the Russian calendar of the time), Emperor Alexander II issued the Emancipation Manifesto, abolishing serfdom in Russia. Approximately 23 million serfs gained personal freedom and a grant of land. All peasants became free rural inhabitants with full rights, while nobles kept their property rights over the land and granted peasants its perpetual use.",
